TEXT -128 -168 Left 3 ;#303 Pulse counting discriminator, steady-frequency sweep (experiment)
TEXT -128 -112 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jQlN2fc7LJc
TEXT -128 -72 Left 2 ;Alan's circuit fed with an unmodulated IF stepped from 50 to 150 kHz, his IF range. Each step settles to one AUDIO level;
TEXT -128 -40 Left 2 ;the levels show how the average voltage tracks the IF frequency (the discriminator transfer curve).
TEXT -128 488 Left 2 ;VIF: unmodulated sine at Alan's measured IF level, 160 mV p-p, frequency set by the stepped parameter fif.
TEXT -128 520 Left 2 ;Assumed (not stated in the video): VCC = 5 V; CLP = 10 nF in place of the stray capacitance and audio-amp bandwidth Alan relies on.
TEXT -128 576 Left 2 !.tran 0 1.5m 0 20n
TEXT -128 616 Left 2 !.step param fif list 50k 75k 100k 125k 150k
TEXT -128 656 Left 2 !.meas tran AUDIO_AVG AVG V(audio) FROM=1m TO=1.5m
